<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Analysis of ColBERT’s Semantic Space</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ColBERT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Khattab and Zaharia (2020)</a></cite> decomposes representations and similarity computation at the token level. Because of this compositional architecture, we hypothesize that ColBERT exhibits a “lightweight” semantic space: without any special re-training, vectors corresponding to each sense of a word would cluster very closely, with only minor variation due to context.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F2.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2112.01488v3/semantic_analysis_legend.svg" id="A1.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/68;" width="476" height="68"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F2.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2112.01488v3/tokens_per_cluster.svg" id="A1.F2.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/447;" width="476" height="447"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Number of distinct tokens appearing in each cluster.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F2.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2112.01488v3/clusters_per_token.svg" id="A1.F2.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/447;" width="476" height="447"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Number of distinct clusters each token appears in.</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Empirical CDFs analyzing semantic properties of MS MARCO token-level embeddings both encoded by ColBERT and randomly generated. The embeddings are partitioned into <math id="A1.F2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{18}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>18</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{18}</annotation></semantics></math> clusters and correspond to roughly 27,000 distinct tokens.</figcaption>
</figure>
