<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dev Results</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A4.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Statistics ‣ Appendix D LoTTE ‣ ColBERTv2: Effective and Efficient Retrieval via Lightweight Late Interaction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> presents out-of-domain evaluation results on the LoTTE dev queries. Continuing the trend we observed in <a href="#S5" title="5 Evaluation ‣ ColBERTv2: Effective and Efficient Retrieval via Lightweight Late Interaction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, ColBERTv2 consistently outperforms all other models we tested.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Licensing and Anonymity</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The original StackExchange post archive is licensed under a Creative Commons BY-SA 4.0 license <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">sta ()</a></cite>. Personal data is removed from the archive before being uploaded, though all posts are public; when we release LoTTE publicly we will include URLs to the original posts for proper attribution as required by the license. The GooAQ dataset is licensed under an Apache license, version 2.0 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Khashabi et al. (2021)</a></cite>. We will also release LoTTE with a CC BY-SA 4.0 license. The search queries can be used for non-commercial research purposes only as per the GooAQ license.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
